  "title": "joins sets subqueries CTEs and recursive queries",
  "status": "source-backed-draft-generation-enabled",
  "concepts": [
    "Join types combine rows with matching predicates or preserve unmatched rows; predicate placement changes outer-join results.",
    "Set operators combine compatible result sets with distinct or duplicate-preserving behavior; ordering is a separate final-query concern.",
    "Subqueries express scalar values, row sets, or existence tests. Correlation and NULL behavior affect both meaning and result cardinality.",
    "A CTE names a query expression for one statement. Recursive CTEs combine anchor and recursive members with a termination condition; a CTE is not automatically materialized or faster."
  ],
